      },
      "category": "Quantitative Aptitude",
      "question": "[Sample] If the price of sugar increases by 25%, by what percentage must a household reduce its consumption so that expenditure remains unchanged?",
      "questionHindi": "[नमूना] यदि चीनी की कीमत में 25% की वृद्धि होती है, तो खपत में कितने प्रतिशत की कमी करनी चाहिए ताकि खर्च अपरिवर्तित रहे?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "18%"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "20%"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "22.5%"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "25%"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "explanation": "Reduction % = [R / (100 + R)] × 100 = (25 / 125) × 100 = 20%.",
      "exam": {
        "name": "SSC CGL",
        "year": 2024,
        "shift": "Shift 1"
      },
      "difficulty": "Easy",
      "source": {
        "pdf": "Sample_percentage.pdf",
        "page": 1,
        "originalQuestionNumber": 1
      },
